{
 "about": "Which clip each shot comes from. 'in' is a fixed in-point in seconds; 'line' asks tools/cutin.py to place the clip so the mouth lands on that finished voice line; 'beat' is the stretch of the clip the shot may use; 'zoom' punches in on the centre; 'matte': 'lens' with zoom, dx and dy sets the shot inside the standard round lens of the blue world; 'fade_in' is frames up from black. 'boil' redraws an ink still every second frame; 'bar_from' marks the shot whose last frame hands its band of light to the cursor. B04, B06 and B08 are made by tools/wind.py from the plates named in timing/wind.json. Run python3 tools/cutin.py after editing. Every person's shots come from that person's own reel, so a face is always from one generation.",
